ST1 with 1 (post-index), 3 and 4 registers -- decoders and semantics.

Completes the LD1/ST1 "multiple structures" family alongside 0072 and 0073.

These five forms differed from the LD1 gaps in an important way: they had NO
`DEF_ISEL` *and* no real decoder. `Decode.cpp` carried

    bool TryDecodeST1_ASISDLSE_R3_3V(const InstData &, Instruction &) {
      return false;
    }

so the decoder REFUSED, and the instruction was fatal (`undecoded instruction`)
rather than a silent no-op. That is the better failure of the two, and it is why
these were lower priority than 0072 even though there are more of them.

Measured encodings that reached the fatal path:
  0x4c9f7314  st1 {v20.16b}, [x24], #16
  0x4c00600a  st1 {v10.16b-v12.16b}, [x0]
  0x4c9f62aa  st1 {v10.16b-v12.16b}, [x21], #48

The stubs are removed from Decode.cpp and real decoders added to Arch.cpp, which
is the convention the already-working forms follow -- `TryDecodeST1_ASISDLSE_
R2_2V` has no stub in Decode.cpp and is defined in Arch.cpp. They delegate:
`TryDecodeSTn` reads the register count out of the opcode, so 3- and 4-register
differ from 1-register only in that count, exactly as the LD1 side already does.

⚠️ Stores need no multi-value return, so no `TTriple`/`TQuad` is involved here.
The sources arrive as ordinary operands and the semantics are `DEF_SEM_VOID_RUN`.
The post-index variants delegate to the non-post-index ones for the same reason
as in 0072/0073: `AddPostIndexMemOp` carries the base-register update and the
lifter applies it after the call.

After this patch every LD1 and ST1 multiple-structures form is implemented. The
`*_ASISDLSEP_R*_R*` register-post-index family (`[Xn], Xm`) remains unhandled;
it also fails loudly, and nothing in the fixtures has been observed to use it.

